message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Independence is necessary but not sufficient: a sovereign, local-hardware test of heterogeneous LLM verification for RAG faithfulness"
authors:
  - family-names: Nelson
    given-names: Clint
    affiliation: "Snake River AI LLC"
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/snake-river-ai/faithfulness-independence"
date-released: "2026-11-04"
version: "0.1.0"
keywords:
  - LLM evaluation
  - verifier independence
  - RAG faithfulness
  - effective sample size
  - heterogeneous panels
abstract: >-
  A sovereign, local-hardware study of heterogeneous LLM verification for retrieval-augmented-generation
  faithfulness. A model-free deterministic checker is statistically independent of an LLM judge (mean pairwise
  error correlation ~= -0.04) yet net-negative on naturally-distributed claims; a single hardened cross-family
  judge matches or beats the heterogeneous panel. Independence is necessary but not sufficient. Judge-panel
  independence preregistration hash-sealed 2026-08-20. Concurrent with and independent of Kohli
  (arXiv:2605.29800) and Kumar (Zenodo 10.5281/zenodo.22368667).
